abstract: >
  Integrated Systems Oncology is a modular computational oncology framework composed
  of four independently validated biological simulation engines: Tumor Evolution,
  Metabolism, Epigenetics, and Synergy, with a master orchestration layer and
  project-wide validation. The framework provides deterministic, reproducible
  simulations of cancer progression, covering clonal evolution, metabolic dynamics,
  epigenetic regulation, and their systems-level interactions. It is designed for
  reproducible computational oncology research, education, and scientific collaboration.
